  "body": "Hi, I just asked chromium people to check this and it's defined in your specs, so for example:\r\n```html\r\n<my-component> </my-component>\r\n```\r\nsets the default slot as \" \", in your definition the default slot can be a text node as well, but I think for the majority this should be a meaningful string, not just a trimmable string, because it can produce confusion and develop problems farther from the web component developer and falling into the developer who uses the web component.\r\n\r\neverybody is used to format HTML code without worrying of meaningless strings as spaces, tabs and new lines.\r\n\r\ncould this definition be changed? or is too much to ask for?\r\n\r\nBest Regards.  ",
